<h1>JSON API</h1>
<p class="lead">OpenFarm publishes a small, read-only JSON API as static files alongside the site. No key, no rate limit from us — please be polite if you crawl, and cache what you use.</p>

<h2 id="licence">Licence and attribution</h2>
<p>Unless a record says otherwise, API content is <a href="https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/">CC BY-SA 4.0</a>.
  Attribute it as “OpenFarm contributors”, keep ShareAlike for adaptations, and keep any upstream credit named on the record
  (for example CC0 rescue imports, Wikidata CC0, Beck et al. 2018 CC BY 4.0).
  Imported records marked <code>license: CC0-1.0</code> stay CC0.
  See <a href="{{ site.repo }}/blob/main/SOURCES.md">SOURCES.md</a> for the full policy.</p>

<h2 id="endpoints">Endpoints</h2>
<p>All paths below are under the site root (on GitHub Pages, prefix <code>/OpenFarm</code>). Examples use that prefix.</p>

<h3><code>GET /api/all.json</code></h3>
<p>A full dump: regions, crops (with varieties and guides), problems, tools, seed sources and companions. Useful for mirrors and research.</p>
<pre><code>curl -sL https://karimogit.github.io/OpenFarm/api/all.json | head</code></pre>
<p>The top-level object includes a <code>generated</code> timestamp (ISO 8601) and a <code>license</code> field. Crop objects include <code>slug</code>, <code>name</code>, <code>url</code>, sources, and nested lists of varieties and guide URLs.</p>

<h3><code>GET /api/guides.json</code></h3>
<p>A compact index of growing guides (crop, region, title, URL, calendar summary, confidence).</p>
<pre><code>curl -sL https://karimogit.github.io/OpenFarm/api/guides.json</code></pre>

<h3><code>GET /api/tools.json</code></h3>
<p>All tools, with category, image licence, sources, and the crops or guides that list them.</p>
<pre><code>curl -sL https://karimogit.github.io/OpenFarm/api/tools.json</code></pre>

<h3><code>GET /crops/&lt;crop&gt;.json</code></h3>
<p>One crop, including varieties and guides. Example: <a href="{{ '/crops/tomato.json' | url }}"><code>/crops/tomato.json</code></a>.</p>
<pre><code>{
  "slug": "tomato",
  "name": "Tomato",
  "url": "/crops/tomato/",
  "license": "CC-BY-SA-4.0",
  "guides": ["/crops/tomato/humid-continental/"]
}</code></pre>
<p class="small muted">Guide <code>url</code> values used to be <code>/guides/&lt;crop&gt;/&lt;region&gt;/</code>. They are now <code>/crops/&lt;crop&gt;/&lt;region&gt;/</code> (and <code>/crops/&lt;crop&gt;/&lt;variety&gt;/&lt;region&gt;/</code> when a variety-specific guide exists). HTML pages at the old paths redirect; the JSON field uses the new URL.</p>

<h3><code>GET /regions/&lt;region&gt;.json</code></h3>
<p>One climate region, with its Köppen classes and the guides that cover it. Example: <a href="{{ '/regions/temperate-oceanic.json' | url }}"><code>/regions/temperate-oceanic.json</code></a>.</p>

<h3><code>GET /zones/&lt;zone&gt;.json</code></h3>
<p>One USDA-style hardiness zone (1a–13b), with temperature bounds and plants whose sourced range includes it. Example: <a href="{{ '/zones/8a.json' | url }}"><code>/zones/8a.json</code></a>. There is also an HTML index at <a href="{{ '/zones/' | url }}">/zones/</a>.</p>

<h2 id="contribute">Contribute via GitHub</h2>
<p>There is no write API. To add or change data, edit the Markdown and YAML in the
  <a href="{{ site.repo }}">GitHub repository</a>:</p>
<ol>
  <li>Open the file (each page has an “Edit this …” button) or copy <a href="{{ site.repo }}/blob/main/content/TEMPLATE.md"><code>content/TEMPLATE.md</code></a> to <code>content/guides/&lt;crop&gt;/&lt;region&gt;.md</code>.</li>
  <li>Fill in frontmatter and at least one real source already listed (or added) in <code>content/sources.yaml</code>.</li>
  <li>Open a pull request. The <code>validate</code> check runs the JSON Schemas in <code>schema/</code>, the licence allowlist, and link/image checks.</li>
</ol>
<p>More detail: <a href="{{ '/help/#api' | url }}">Help</a>, <a href="{{ '/contribute/' | url }}">About</a>, and <a href="{{ site.repo }}/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md">CONTRIBUTING.md</a>.</p>
</article>
